>>
>> I simply wanted to test CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_POWERSAVE=3Dy and
>> keep the rest.
>
> But it is not clear to us whether or not your system has regressed
> with respect to 4.5, which is the whole point of this thread.  Do you
> see a regression here?
>
> J=C3=B6rg in particular is saying that he sees the problem with both
> performance and powersave settings.  What about you?

I have only tested with 4.6-rc1.
My 4.5 kernel has no CONFIG_X86_MSR=3Dm which is mandatory for turbostat.

With CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_POWERSAVE=3Dy and without your
simplified revert-patch.
The values of Bzy_MHz look good for me.

CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_PERFORMANCE=3Dy is somehow showing higher
values than TSC_MHz.
Not sure if this really make sense if TSC_MHz is a max-value (which I
don't know it is).

- Sedat -

